{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1989"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge science/biology","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/science__biology.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",450],["+","That voyage nearly did not happen: Darwin's father opposed it, and it was his uncle, the pottery manufacturer Josiah Wedgwood II, who in 1831 talked him round, so that the 22-year-old could sail as the ship's naturalist. "],["=",146],["+","The science of sorting living things into such ranked categories is called taxonomy, and Linnaeus is regarded as its father. "],["=",461]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",432],["+","Beinahe hätte diese Reise nicht stattgefunden: Darwins Vater war dagegen, und erst sein Onkel, der Keramikfabrikant Josiah Wedgwood II, stimmte ihn 1831 um, sodass der 22-Jährige als Naturforscher an Bord gehen konnte. "],["=",146],["+","Die Wissenschaft, Lebewesen in solche Rangstufen einzuordnen, heißt Taxonomie, und Linné gilt als ihr Vater. "],["=",449]]}]},
